Krita Nova 42 - import Photoshop brushes (.abr) as ready-to-use brushes

The brush presets (the presets popup of the brush panel / toolbar, the Brush
Presets docker and the brush editor's preset list) get an "Import Photoshop
Brushes..." button. It opens one or more .abr files and makes every brush of
a file a Pixel brush preset, tagged with the file's name:

- The tips are imported as Krita always did (the .abr is copied into the
  resource folder and becomes a storage of brush tips); importing the same
  file again reuses it, a different file with the same name gets "name (2)".
- From the brush settings of the file (the "desc" section of Photoshop 6+
  brush files): name; the tip (round computed tips become auto brushes with
  their hardness and roundness, sampled tips use their imported tip, scaled
  to the brush's diameter); angle, roundness, spacing; Shape Dynamics: size
  jitter and size control (fade, pen pressure, pen tilt, stylus wheel) with
  its minimum diameter, angle jitter and angle control (also rotation,
  initial direction, direction); Scattering (amount, both axes, control);
  Transfer: opacity and flow jitter and control.
- Not imported: texture, dual brush, color dynamics, count, noise, wet edges.
- Files without settings (Photoshop 5 and older, or tips only) get one preset
  per tip.

New plugin plugins/extensions/photoshopbrushes: the action
"import_photoshop_brushes" (Settings category) and KisAbrPresetImporter (a
reader for Photoshop's action descriptors and the preset builder, using the
paintop option data of libpaintop). KisPresetChooser: the button triggers
that action.
